,"bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/figures/m828a1f.gif","alt":"The figure shows changes in obesity prevalence from the period 1998-2003 to the period 2003-2008 among U.S. children aged 2-4 years, by race/ethnicity, based on date from the Pediatric Nutrition Surveillance System. Overall, obesity prevalence among these low-income, preschool-aged children enrolled in federally funded nutrition programs increased steadily from 12.4% in 1998 to 14.5% in 2003, but subsequently remained essentially the same, with a 14.6% prevalence in 2008. Obesity increased across all racial/ethnic groups during 1998-2003, with the exception of Asian/Pacific Islander children. However, during 2003-2008, obesity remained stable among all groups except American Indian/Alaska Native children. In 2008, prevalence was highest among American Indian/Alaska Native (21.2%) and Hispanic (18.5%) children, and lowest among non-Hispanic white (12.6%), non-Hispanic black (11.8%), and Asian/Pacific Islander (12.3%) children.","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":521,"renderedHeight":372,"naturalWidth":521,"naturalHeight":372,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"TOO_LONG","altReason":"alt text is 939 characters — consider a caption or description","bytes":11195},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/images/spacer.gif","alt":" ","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":false,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":10,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"DECORATIVE","altReason":"alt=\"\" (decorative)","bytes":821},{"src":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/headers_footers/images/spacer1.gif","alt":"","hasAlt":true,"isDecorative":true,"isMissingAlt":false,"ariaHidden":false,"rolePresentation":false,"renderedWidth":1,"renderedHeight":1,"naturalWidth":10,"naturalHeight":10,"loading":null,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"D